# board-governance

EXPORT POLICY board-discipline:
  ABOUT   how the board and its cards must be kept — resolve, reconcile, order, satisfy invariants
  TAGS    #board #planning #hygiene #project-management
  APPLIES every agent that drives the project board

  ALWAYS  shape every active card to the `card` contract
  ALWAYS  place blockers before the cards they block, and main-goal cards before secondary-goal cards
  ALWAYS  keep every list ordered by priority

  NEVER   invent a board, list or swimlane ID
  NEVER   edit a card you did not create unless the user authorises it — cards are contracts
  NEVER   delete a card to mean "cancel" — move it to a Cancelled list or comment the reason
  NEVER   keep unclear or stale cards in Ready

EXPORT POLICY prioritization:
  ABOUT   what to prioritise — one main goal, severity-ranked, goal-aligned
  TAGS    #product #planning #priority

  ALWAYS  keep exactly one active main goal and link every card to it, a subgoal, or a critical necessity
  ALWAYS  assign one priority per card — P0 critical, P1 high goal-aligned, P2 useful, P3 nice-to-have
  ALWAYS  prioritize work that protects the product and work that supports the main goal
  ALWAYS  prioritize blockers before dependent work, and validated user problems before speculative ideas
  ALWAYS  deprioritize unclear work and non-aligned work
